# Multi-API Key Configuration for Debatable Project
# This file shows how to configure multiple API keys for better reliability and accuracy

# ============================================================================
# GROQ API KEYS - Multiple Key Support
# ============================================================================
# Option 1: Single Key (backward compatible)
GROQ_API_KEY=your-single-groq-key-here

# Option 2: Multiple Numbered Keys (recommended)
# Uncomment and fill in your Groq API keys from https://console.groq.com
GROQ_API_KEY_1=your-first-groq-key
GROQ_API_KEY_2=your-second-groq-key
GROQ_API_KEY_3=your-third-groq-key

# Option 3: Comma-separated Keys
# Alternatively, you can provide all keys in one variable (comma-separated)
# GROQ_API_KEYS=key1,key2,key3

# ============================================================================
# OPENAI API KEYS - Used for accurate analysis and as Groq fallback
# ============================================================================
OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-key-here
# OPENAI_API_KEY_1=your-openai-key-1
# OPENAI_API_KEY_2=your-openai-key-2
# Optional: override default chat model (default: gpt-4o-mini)
# OPENAI_CHAT_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# ============================================================================
# SOCIAL LOGIN (Google & Apple)
# ============================================================================
# Google OAuth - create at https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# Authorized redirect URI: http://localhost:8000/auth/google/callback
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-google-client-secret
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8000/auth/google/callback

# Apple Sign In - https://developer.apple.com/account/resources/identifiers/list/serviceId
# APPLE_CLIENT_ID=com.yourapp.web
# APPLE_TEAM_ID=your-team-id
# APPLE_KEY_ID=your-key-id
# APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----"
# APPLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8000/auth/apple/callback

# Frontend URL used after OAuth callback
# FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ============================================================================
# ANTHROPIC API KEYS - For future multi-provider support
# ============================================================================
# Uncomment to use Anthropic (Claude) as fallback or additional provider
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_1=your-anthropic-key-1
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_2=your-anthropic-key-2

# ============================================================================
# JWT Configuration
# ============================================================================
SECRET_KEY=your-secret-key-change-in-production

# ============================================================================
# How to Get Multiple API Keys
# ============================================================================
# 1. Groq (Primary Provider)
#    - Go to https://console.groq.com
#    - Create multiple API keys under your account
#    - Add them as GROQ_API_KEY_1, GROQ_API_KEY_2, etc.
#
# 2. Why Multiple Keys?
#    - Rate limit management: Distribute requests across keys
#    - Failover capability: If one key fails, system tries another
#    - Improved reliability: Better handling of API outages
#    - Load balancing: Even distribution of API calls
#    - Cost optimization: Spread usage across budget tiers

# ============================================================================
# Configuration Priority
# ============================================================================
# The system will load keys in this order:
# 1. GROQ_API_KEY (single key, backward compatible)
# 2. GROQ_API_KEY_1, GROQ_API_KEY_2, GROQ_API_KEY_3, etc. (numbered keys)
# 3. GROQ_API_KEYS (comma-separated keys)
# Duplicate keys are automatically removed.
